  DEFENDING ARMY

  Giovanna stood ready at the head of her thousands.  Guerin marched with 
his loyal troops, jaws set in terrible resolution.
  The army of Giovanna used magic to aid their cause.  Magical phantasmal 
armies fought with hers soldiers.  The Skeletal Armies led by 
Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) marched into battle with a fanatical fervor.  Giovanna 
wielded her Sword Excalibur.  She stepped forward and challenged Guerin 
(#18) to personal combat.  Guerin declined to enter combat.
  The forces commanded by Guerin were dismayed by his faint-heartedness.  
They marched on, though with lessened confidence.  His soldiers, with no 
camels for the tortuous desert, suffered from thirst.  Giovanna's luck 
seemed to be running low, as the engagement's unforeseen timing caught her 
soldiers somewhat unprepared.  Guerin's men thus gained a significant edge.  
As the desperate battle developed, the tactical wit of Guerin and Giovanna 
appeared to be evenly matched and neither leader could gain a tactical 
advantage.
  Calling upon her magical powers of Oratory, Giovanna gave a rousing speech 
to her army, raising their morale.  She held aloft her Sword Excalibur and 
the Humans were virtually hypnotized!  The Elves commanded by Giovanna were 
not impressed by her lack of leadership ability.
  On the left outside wing, the Crack 274th Legion sang their heroic 
ballads, inspired with a fanatical fury by their exalted King.  They were 
arrayed against the Crack 108th Bowmen.  The 274th Legion battled the 108th 
Bowmen and determinedly plowed into their opponents.
  In the interior lines, the 177th Legion faced the 292nd Legion.  Here, 
after some fighting, the commander of the 292nd Legion waved a white flag 
and offered his sword to the enemy commander.  But just as he reached out to 
accept it, he was treacherously decapitated!  At this signal, the 292nd 
Legion charged forward in a surprise attack.  The 177th Legion fought the 
292nd Legion and neither army could gain an advantage over the other.
  In the interior front, the Elite 259th Legion were aided by a Thunderbird 
who descended from the stars to aid their Divine cause, and were elevated to 
fanaticism by its divine splendor.  They faced the Elite 240th Skeletal 
Bowmen, who were encouraged to selfless fanatiscm by Guerin, their heroic 
First Elder of Elvenkind.  The horses of the 185th Light Cavalry were 
spooked by the Beasts they were faced with.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons 
swooped down on the 185th Light Cavalry and attacked without mercy.  In this 
engagement, the 259th Legion feigned retreat, hoping to lure the enemy into 
more suitable ground.  But the ruse backfired when some of the soldiers 
panicked, and the 259th Legion milled about in confusion.
  But then the tide of battle reversed.  The 240th Skeletal Bowmen's luck 
turned horrible!  A meteor fell upon the 240th Skeletal Bowmen and killed 
many soldiers.  The 259th Legion fought the 240th Skeletal Bowmen and 
gradually gave ground.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 186th Legion were arrayed against the 
Green 209th Warg Riders.  The 186th Legion fought with the 209th Warg Riders 
and squashed them like rotten tomatoes.
  In the interior front, the 299th Legion sang out their fiery battle hymns, 
inspired with a fanatical fury by their exalted King.  They faced the Elite 
241st Bowmen.  In this sector, the men of the 241st Bowmen indulged in 
plundering before the contest was over, which weakened their numbers a 
little.  The 299th Legion fought the 241st Bowmen and steadily advanced 
against them.
  On the right wing, the Veteran 275th Legion faced the Crack 110th Bowmen.  
In this match, the contest was an uneventful slugfest which was decided by 
the courage of the soldiers in hand-to-hand combat.  The 275th Legion fought 
the 110th Bowmen and aggressively knifed into them.
  The forces of Giovanna broke through and were victorious.  The 274th 
Legion scattered the 108th Bowmen in all directions.  The 186th Legion slew 
the 209th Warg Riders almost to a man.  The 299th Legion demolished the 
241st Bowmen.  The 331st Bowmen chased after the enemy and were driven off 
by the 110th Bowmen after a hard-fought rearguard battle.  The 185th 
Light Cavalry overtook the enemy in their panicky retreat and annihilated 
the 292nd Legion.  The 243rd Light Cavalry gave chase and destroyed the 
110th Bowmen.
  Giovanna's host ended the campaign successfully and conquered the province 
of Rejaf.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  the 274th Legion 
proved its valor during the battle and we now rank it an Elite unit.  The 
299th Legion was greatly buoyed by the victory.  We now designate it a proud 
Veteran unit.  The 331st Bowmen fought determinedly during the battle and 
came through with flying colors.  We can now rank it a Veteran unit.  Guerin 
retired to Quantara Roo, defeated but not discouraged.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)ian 
empire marched on the Forest province of Marigold, a land defended by the 
soldiers of Giovanna.  Marigold was overrun by Alaric (#22)'s host.  Alaric 
leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 2 Legion and 1 Light Cavalry.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  Giovanna marched her forces 
into Maplehaven (#1502).
  Kajaani was magically blessed and prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 
276th Light Cavalry were Blessed and permanently destroyed.
  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Maplehaven, 
a Forest area owned by Giovanna.  Teleko (#72) commanded the attacking 
armies.  The defenders were led by Giovanna.  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

