  DEFENDING ARMY

  Kari led her armies into the fray.  No generals were present to lead the 
forces of Giovanna.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Kari (#81)'s fortunes took a terrible turn for the worse 
when some of her troops rebelled against her strict discipline and refused 
to enter battle.  As the struggle developed, the tactical wit of the acting 
commander and Kari seemed to be evenly matched.

  Across the whole front, the 55th Garrison were arrayed against the 54th 
Garrison, who sang out their battle hymns, infused with a spirit of holy, 
fanatical elan by their exalted King.  The 55th Garrison battled with the 
54th Garrison and were mowed down like sheep.
  The acting commander's great horde overwhelmed the army of Uga-Buga Makumb 
(#1) and took the field, scattering their enemies.  The 54th Garrison 
annihilated the 55th Garrison.
  The host of the attacking Kingdom was defeated and driven out of Cascadia. 
Her forces completely destroyed, Kari (#81) fled frightened and alone to 
Marigold.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Maicuru, a 
Jungle area owned by Giovanna.  Maicuru was conquered by Pascal (#78)'s 
host.  Pascal leads approximately 3 Legion and 1 Chariots.
  Kurator went back to Valhalla, having tried his best to fulfill his 
assignments.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Giovanna for this year.


  Giovanna treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Giovanna treated with her 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Giovanna treated with her ally Hokuto (#4).
Giovanna treated with her ally Prometeo (#5).  Giovanna treated with her 
ally II Kahn (#6).  Giovanna treated with her ally Circe (#8).  Giovanna 
treated with her ally Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  The 182nd Trolls experienced a disastrous raiding attempt in Moussoro and 
sank to Depleted quality.  The 182nd Trolls laid down their swords and quit 
the mercenary life.
  Newly come from Elkhome is the 323rd Trolls, which army is seeking a liege 
in Maplehaven.


  Here is the financial report for Giovanna's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 27 gold in revenue.  16 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 79th Were-Beasts trained well and improved in quality.  33 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Giovanna was left with 18 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Rolando
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I marched on Maplehaven (#1502) with my command.  Maplehaven 
had an illusion cast upon it.  It was actually a Forest province.

  Giovanna ordered an invasion force into the adjacent Forest province of 
Maplehaven, owned by Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1).  Rolando's 
forces took Maplehaven without any major battles.  Maplehaven was found to 
have a tax base of 6 gold.
  In early summer, I cancelled my move to Sageleaf in order to fight for the 
province of Maplehaven.  Instead, I practiced my Spying well, and even 
consulted an astrologer, but could not improve my Spying.
  With the coming of the late summer season, I cast a Bless spell.  
Maplehaven was magically blessed and prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 
321st Eagles were Blessed and permanently destroyed.  My experience raised 
my prowess in White Magic.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into fall.  I could not cast Tornado on 
Pearlgate because I needed to be in or next to the target province.  
Instead, I practiced my Spying diligently for months, but could make no 
headway.
  The fall cooled into early winter.  I wasn't in Sageleaf so I utilized my 
covert skills to secretly observe happenings in Maplehaven and reported the 
following information.  The province of Maplehaven belongs to Giovanna.  
Listening to the stories of travellers and merchants, one can deduce the 
rulership of surrounding provinces: Elkhome- no one.
  Approximate Taxation: 3
  The following elements are present in Maplehaven:  Giovanna (a Human 
worshipped for White Magic) is here.  Giovanna leads approximately 3 Bowmen, 8
Legion, 3 Light Cavalry and 2 Camel Corps.  Isis (a Elf renowned for Element 
Magic) is here.
  I also kept tabs on the characters in Maplehaven and any further news is 
in the General Intelligence Report.

  Thy humble servant,   Rolando


From: Watson, Squire to Hakim
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to spring, and Hakim prepared to carry out his 
urgent assignments.  He cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies 
were formed for Giovanna.
  During early summer, Hakim enlisted the 79th Were-Beasts in Kajaani to 
serve Hakim.
  With the coming of the late summer season Hakim marched on Maplehaven 
(#1502) with his formidable forces.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  Hakim boldly marched his 
forces into Sageleaf (#1602).

  Giovanna's forces initiated a campaign of conquest in Sageleaf, a Forest 
province owing allegiance to Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Hakim's 
forces experienced little resistance in Sageleaf and Hakim there established 
our rule.  Sageleaf was discovered to have a tax base of 5 gold.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Hakim's Bless spell fizzled and 
Hakim was left with his face covered with psycho-kinetic goo.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Hakim


From: Kurator
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I cast a Bless spell.  Kajaani was magically blessed and 
prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 20th Legion, the 230th Legion and 
the 244th Light Cavalry were Blessed and permanently destroyed.
  In early summer, I moved into Maplehaven.  I marched along some previously 
unexplored paths, raising our exploration knowledge to 100%.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer arrived.  I tried to practice my 
Druidism, but the task seemed beyond my natural ability.
  The hot days of summer surrendered to a colorful fall.  I journeyed to 
Damnonia.  While on the march, I took an interest in the terrain of Damnonia,
exploring some unknown territory.  We have now explored 100% of Damnonia.  I 
saw no wandering monster.
  With the advent of the early winter season I unsheathed my weapon and 
entered the Tomb warily.  I encountered the Ice Devil.  Chanting my silver 
words of magic into a mighty Holy Symbol spell, I waved my arms.  A golden 
mist in the shape of a cross formed around me.  The spell made the Ice Devil 
moan in excruciating pain and walloped the Ice Devil with 9 damage points.  
The Ice Devil's spell was disrupted by the event.  The Ice Devil chanted its 
strange words of magic and cast a Charm spell but the spell seemed 
ineffective against me.
  I loped along steadily and closed to bow range.  The Ice Devil waved its 
hands and gestured rhythmically, meaning to cast a Psychic Blast spell, but 
it went awry and a rabbit tumbled out of its sleeve instead.  I took careful 
aim and fired an arrow at the Ice Devil and damaged the Ice Devil, scoring 1 
damage points.  Drawing back with all my strength, I shot an arrow at 
the Ice Devil and scored on the Ice Devil, inflicting 2 points of damage.  I 
shot an arrow at the Ice Devil and missed by a mile.  The Ice Devil thought 
to cast an Ice Suspension spell, but dropped a needed material component 
before the Ice Devil could make its attempt.
  I charged into the melee.  The Ice Devil daringly slashed at me but its 
aim was slightly off the mark.  I maneuvered to a good attacking vantage.  
Then I swang at the Ice Devil and scored 1 damage points on the Ice Devil.
  The Ice Devil swang at me but I evaded the claws.  I swang at 
the Ice Devil and inflicted 5 damage points.  Hoping to exploit a gap in 
Kurator's protection, the Ice Devil slashed at me and would have struck me 
if I hadn't sidestepped.  I faked one way, then switched over and swang at 
the Ice Devil and walloped the Ice Devil with 3 damage points.
  The Ice Devil attacked me but its claws whiffed harmlessly through the 
air.  I swang at the Ice Devil and missed.  The Ice Devil swang at its 
nemesis but its aim was just off.  I then thrust at the Ice Devil but 
the Ice Devil dodged the blow.  The Ice Devil swang at me and would have 
struck me if I hadn't sidestepped just then.  I whirled around and swang at 
the Ice Devil and damaged the Ice Devil, scoring 3 damage points.
  The Ice Devil maneuvered to a better defensive vantage.  Then 
the Ice Devil swang at me but its claws whiffed harmlessly through the air.  
I acrobatically flipped over the Ice Devil and thrust at the Ice Devil and 
missed by a mile.  Undaunted, the Ice Devil swang at me but its aim was 
slightly off.  I swang at the Ice Devil but the Ice Devil dodged the blow.
  The Ice Devil feinted one way, then switched over and treacherously swang 
at me and would have hit me if I hadn't ducked just then.  I circled left 
and attacked the Ice Devil but my sword whiffed harmlessly through the air.  
The Ice Devil slashed at me and missed badly.  I summoned all my will and 
bravely thrust at my fearsome enemy but my aim was just off the mark.
  The Ice Devil forced back me with its aggressive tactics.  The Ice Devil 
then slashed at me but I dodged the claws.  I feigned panic, then pivoted 
and arrogantly swang at the Ice Devil and scored on the Ice Devil, 
inflicting 1 points of damage.  The Ice Devil swang at me and would have 
struck me if I hadn't ducked just then.  I maneuvered to a better attacking 
vantage.  Then I thrust at the Ice Devil and scored 2 damage points on 
the Ice Devil.  The Ice Devil dropped to the ground, fatally pierced.  I 
shifted my attention to the hoard of the Ice Devil.  I bagged the Large 
Hoard of Gold.  I took 19 gold from the treasure of the Ice Devil.
  While scouting the Tomb, I saw a Tome which seemed to be of a magical 
nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Tome, saying "The Tome will cast a Flood spell 
for a character who kneels before the Tome in prayer.  The Flood spell will 
take effect on this province.  You must pay 2 gold each time the Tome is 
used (to show that you accept these terms, a character must give two Scout 
orders when he Searches this feature.)"  I saw no wandering monster.
  I went back to Valhalla, having tried my best to fulfill my assignments.


  Thy humble servant,   Kurator


From: Tiffany
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cast a spell giving magical powers of oratory to Giovanna.
  In early summer, I travelled to Moussoro.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer came.  I enlisted the 
113th Camel Corps in Moussoro to serve me.
  With the coming of the fall season I attempted an illegal move.  I tried 
to move from Moussoro to Kajaani, but provincial flooding and insufficient 
transport thwarted the move.  Instead, I practiced my Exploring well, and 
even consulted a palm reader, but could not improve my Exploring.
  In early winter, I moved into Pearlgate (#1703) with my army.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
