  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 184th Skeletal Bowmen in reserve.  Alaric stood 
ready at the head of his thousands.  Standing at the ready with my warriors 
was I.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  As per Alaric (#22)'s usual good fortune, I was 
recovering from injuries sustained in a minor engagement, and Alaric thus 
obtained an edge.  On the other hand his tactical maneuvers did not succeed 
as expected against Tiffany's clever counterstrokes, and his men entered 
battle with a slight tactical disadvantage.
  Giovanna's troops swore to fight like tigers for their fatherland.
  Across the whole front, the Veteran 219th Skeletal Legion were arrayed 
against the Green 113th Camel Corps.  The 144th Skeletal Legion and the 
143rd Skeletal Light Cavalry flanked the enemy lines and charged in with 
full strength.  The nervous horses of the 143rd Skeletal Light Cavalry were 
frightened by the terrible Beasts they beheld.  The 219th Skeletal Legion 
fought with the 113th Camel Corps and crushed their heads as if they were 
eggshells.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Alaric as they broke 
through at a crucial moment.  The 219th Skeletal Legion destroyed the 113th 
Camel Corps.
  Alaric's campaign effected the conquest of Pearlgate.  My forces 
completely destroyed, I fled frightened and alone to Moussoro.

  Thy humble servant,   Tiffany


From: Drake
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to fragrant spring, and I prepared to carry out my urgent 
assignments.  I moved into Kajaani (#1603) with my army.
  In early summer, I marched my forces into Maplehaven (#1502).
  With the coming of the late summer season I marched on Elkhome (#1501) 
with my forces.

  Giovanna's forces initiated a campaign of conquest directed at Elkhome, a 
Forest province owing its allegiance to the provincial Ent chieftain.  I was 
in command of the invading armies.  The defenders were commanded by the 
provincial Ent chieftain.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Elkhome (1501):

 248th/V  
  Lt Cav  
 07 
----------
 вввGCввв 
 167th/A  
   Ents   
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  I led my armies boldly into the battle.  No generals were present to lead 
the forces of the provincial Ent chieftain.
  I was not at all lucky this time, because a strong wind blew against my 
men's eyes, giving the provincial Ent chieftain's host a small edge.  As the 
battle developed, the tactical abilities of the provincial Ent chieftain and 
I appeared evenly matched and neither leader could achieve a tactical 
advantage.

  Across the whole front, the Veteran 248th Light Cavalry faced the 167th 
Ents.  The 248th Light Cavalry fought the 167th Ents and were knocked out of 
the fight by the enemy's ferocious charge.
  The forces of the provincial Ent chieftain broke through the lines of 
their enemy and were victorious.  The 167th Ents demolished the 248th 
Light Cavalry.
  The attacking Kingdom was defeated and forced out of Elkhome.  My forces 
completely destroyed, I fled frightened and alone to Maplehaven.
  With the advent of the fall season, I could not search the Glade because 
it is in another province.  So, I worked hard on my Necromancy but was 
thwarted in my self-improvement efforts.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I could not search the Glade 
because it is in another province.  Instead, I tried hard to improve my 
Navigation, but I practiced in vain.

  Thy humble servant,   Drake


From: Watson, Squire to Isis
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to spring, and Isis made ready to carry out her urgent 
orders.  She tried an Oratory spell, but botched it.
  With the coming of the early summer season, Isis cast a Tornado spell.  
Magical tornadoes hit the defenders of Pearlgate.  The Tornado affected no 
armies in Pearlgate.
  In late summer, Isis cast a Flood spell and Kajaani was magically flooded.
  The summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Isis journeyed to Maplehaven.  
She saw no monster.
  With the coming of the early winter season Isis's Bless spell fizzled and 
Isis was left covered with psycho-kinetic goo.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Isis


From: Bairn
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were 
formed for Giovanna.  Bairn's efforts raised my prowess in Illusions.
  With the coming of the early summer season, I attempted a Tornado spell, 
but botched it.
  Midsummer's night passed and a hot late summer arrived.  I rode into 
Maplehaven.
  During fall, I utilized my fine covert skills to secretly observe 
happenings in Maplehaven and reported the following information.
  Approximate Taxation: 9
  The following elements are present in Maplehaven:  Giovanna (a Human 
worshipped for White Magic) is here.  Rolando (a Human famous for White 
Magic) is here.
  I also kept tabs on the characters in Maplehaven and any further news is 
in the General Intelligence Report.

  The fall cooled into early winter.  I spied on Maplehaven.  Here is my 
report:  the province of Maplehaven belongs to Giovanna.  Listening to the 
stories of wanderers and merchants, one can deduce the ownership of 
surrounding provinces: Elkhome- no one.
  Approximate Taxation: 9
  The following elements are present in Maplehaven:  Giovanna (a Human 
worshipped for White Magic) is here.  Giovanna leads approximately 2 Bowmen, 8
Legion, 3 Light Cavalry and 1 Camel Corps.  Rolando (a Human famous for 
White Magic) is here.  Rolando leads approximately 1 Legion.  Isis (a Elf 
renowned for Element Magic) is here.
  I also kept tabs on the characters in Maplehaven and any further news is 
in the General Intelligence Report.

  Thy humble servant,   Bairn


From: Adhemar
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I travelled to Quantara Roo.  Turning to the southwest, one can 
see a Sea area, which is known as Mercia (#1304).  It is populated by Whales 
and Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll rules there.  They can call on an 
army of Whales to defend their territory.  To the west lies a rich Forest 
area called Bronzeleaf (#1303), populated by Humans.  It is ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Their Human warriors fight in the style 
of Legion.  I discovered an interesting feature in Quantara Roo: a Cavern 
(#31) occupied by the Imp.  Legend says the Shrunken-Head Amulet is hidden 
here.  Evil magic-users say that the Imp is a weak minor devil who often 
will act as a "familiar", or magical companion, for evil characters.  I 
discovered a previously unheard of Crypt (#120) in Quantara Roo, inhabited 
by the Ice Devil.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  Legend has it 
that the Ice Devil is an extraordinarily cruel, cold and very powerful devil 
with magical powers.  In my travels, I encountered no monsters.
  In early summer, I explored Quantara Roo and now 100% of it has been 
explored.  I was informed by some peasants of a feature in Quantara Roo, a 
Sacred Rock (#52) inhabited by the Sphinx.  The Sphinx has already been 
killed; the Sacred Rock, sacked and looted.  While adventuring, I 
encountered no wandering monsters.
  With the advent of the late summer season, I journeyed to Sherwood.  West 
of here lies the province of Peachwood (#1202), ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  It is known to be a Forest province 
inhabited by Ents.  If need be, they can call on an army of Ents to defend 
their territory.  Viewing the northwestern horizon, a man can see a Forest 
province called Gnarlia (#1301).  It is said that 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll reigns there.  It is known to be occupied 
by Humans.  Their Human warriors array themselves in the style of Bowmen and 
Light Cavalry.  I found a Hollow Tree (#6) in Sherwood, occupied by 
the Centaur.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  Wood-Elves say that 
the Centaur is a cross-breed, with the body of a man and the trunk and legs 
of a horse.  He is a good archer and is usually friendly.  During my travels 
this season, I was faced with a Spectre.  I ran furiously and fled from the 
encounter.

  The sultry days of summer surrendered to fall.  I explored Sherwood 
thoroughly, leaving no stone unturned, and our exploration level there has 
risen to 68%.  I discovered an interesting feature in Sherwood: a Hollow 
Tree (#11) occupied by the Treant.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  
The Treant is a large tree capable of moving its limbs and arms much as a 
man does.  I saw no monster.
  With the coming of the early winter season I wandered freely about 
Sherwood, exploring its mysteries, and raising our exploration level in 
Sherwood to 100%.  I saw no marauding monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Adhemar


